    "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine how many questions Frank answered correctly. Let's define the variables first:\n\n- Let \\( x \\) be the number of questions Frank answered correctly.\n- Let \\( y \\) be the number of questions Frank answered incorrectly.\n\nFrom the problem, we know two things:\n1. Frank answered a total of 80 questions.\n2. Frank scored a total of 232 points.\n\nWe can set up the following system of equations based on the information given:\n\n1. \\( x + y = 80 \\)\n2. \\( 5x - 2y = 232 \\)\n\nFirst, we solve the first equation for \\( y \\):\n\n\\[\ny = 80 - x\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( y = 80 - x \\) into the second equation:\n\n\\[\n5x - 2(80 - x) = 232\n\\]\n\nSimplify and solve for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\n5x - 160 + 2x = 232\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\n7x - 160 = 232\n\\]\n\nAdd 160 to both sides:\n\n\\[\n7x = 392\n\\]\n\nDivide by 7:\n\n\\[\nx = 56\n\\]\n\nSo, Frank answered \\( 56 \\) questions correctly. To verify, we calculate the number of incorrect answers \\( y \\):\n\n\\[\ny = 80 - x = 80 - 56 = 24\n\\]\n\nNow, we check the total score:\n\n\\[\n5(56) - 2(24) = 280 - 48 = 232\n\\]\n\nThe calculations confirm that Frank's score is indeed 232 points. Therefore, the number of questions Frank answered correctly is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{56}\n\\]",
